Start with `max_step`. For a sample whose material enables motion limiting, compute Euclidean velocity norm plus the Frobenius gradient norm multiplied by `cell_width² / 4`. If this denominator is positive, limit the result by `cell_width / denominator`; a zero denominator adds no limit. For a non-damaged sample with a deformation limit, also limit by that value. Damaged samples ignore only the deformation limit. Empty samples return `max_step`. Inputs must not be mutated.

